# Files that live in the repo but must NOT be served on the website.
#
# Syntax is the same as .gitignore. Wrangler applies this when it uploads, so
# anything listed here never reaches the edge — it is not hidden, it is absent.
# Nothing here is deleted from the repo; you keep every file locally and on
# GitHub exactly as before.
#
# NOTE: trailing comments are not supported. `foo.png  # unused` would be read
# as a pattern containing the words, so keep comments on their own lines.
#
# Do NOT add these, the live site needs them:
#   index.html, 404.html, favicon.ico, storefront.jpg (used 4x),
#   site.webmanifest, assets/**, and robots.txt + sitemap.xml, which Google
#   reads directly.

# THE IMPORTANT ONE. The build server clones the repo, so .git ends up sitting
# in the directory that gets uploaded. Serving it publishes the whole repository
# — every commit, the full history — because .git/index and the pack files are
# enough to reconstruct it with off-the-shelf tools. Verified live before this
# was added: /.git/config, /.git/HEAD, /.git/index and /.git/logs/HEAD all
# returned 200 on jagdambeystore.com.
#
# This stays excluded no matter what else changes, and it is NOT made safe by
# making the GitHub repo private — the website would still serve it.
.git/

# The Worker config itself. Serving it publishes the Worker's name and setup;
# caught by a local test that found /wrangler.jsonc returning 1861 bytes.
wrangler.jsonc
wrangler.toml
wrangler.json

# Wrangler's local state directory. It lands INSIDE the assets directory, so
# without this a build that creates it would publish it.
.wrangler/

# Never publish credentials, if one is ever added locally by mistake.
.env
*.token

# Owner documentation. Written for whoever maintains the shop's site, and of no
# use to a visitor who lands on it.
*.md
README.txt

# Build and setup scripts. These describe how the site is put together and how
# the domain is switched, which is not something to hand to the public.
build-schema.js
go-live.py
set-domain.py

# Unused leftovers.
# favicon.png is superseded by favicon.ico and nothing links to it.
# jagdambey-banner.png is 1.26 MB and referenced nowhere; the banner actually
# in use is assets/brand/banner.png.
favicon.png
jagdambey-banner.png

# Repo housekeeping, irrelevant to a browser.
.gitignore
